## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical tenant isolation at the messaging layer using Pub/Sub and IAM Conditions.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub isolation, IAM Conditions, per-tenant topics
- Dedicated service accounts per tenant
- Network controls to prevent egress
- CI validation with synthetic tenants

## Code Example
```javascript
// Binding example (pseudo)
{
  "bindings": [
    {
      "role": "roles/pubsub.publisher",
      "members": ["serviceAccount:tenant-sa@example.com"],
      "condition": {
        "title": "TenantTopicIsolation",
        "expression": "resource.name.startsWith(\"projects/PROJECT_ID/topics/tenant-\" + tenantId)"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Explain the need for tamper-evident logs in multi-tenant environments and how this affects compliance and incident response.

## Key Concepts
- Tamper-evident logging and hash chaining
- Rekor/Cosign for provenance attestations
- CMEK-protected destinations and per-tenant partitioning
- Minimise performance impact and ensure cross-tenant isolation
- Incident response with rollback and replay-safe state

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: basic hash chaining for logs
const crypto = require('crypto');
function hashChain(prev, entry){ 
  const data = (prev || '') + JSON.stringify(entry);
  return crypto.createHash('sha256').update(data).digest('hex');
}
```

